{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 16, :comments ["<b>And this people shall rise up, etc.</b> It is difficult: is this a ״rising up״ for them? Is not whoring after foreign gods rather a descent and a degradation for them? But perhaps it intends to say along the lines of His saying (Deuteronomy 32:15): ״וַיִּשְׁמַן יְשֻׁרוּן וַיִּבְעָט״ — and it says ״וְקָם הָעָם״, meaning, it had a rising up in the world through inheritance of the land, and wealth and honor, and it grew fat; and from this resulted its kicking and whoring after, etc. And so He says nearby (Deuteronomy 31:19): ״כִּתְבוּ לָכֶם אֶת הַשִּׁירָה הַזֹּאת וְגוֹ׳ כִּי אֲבִיאֶנּוּ וְגוֹ׳ וְאָכַל וְשָׂבַע וְדָשֵׁן וּפָנָה אֶל אֱלֹהִים אֲחֵרִים״, etc. — behold, He preceded ״sated״ and ״grown fat״ before ״turned״; likewise in the matter before us He preceded saying ״וְקָם״ and afterwards ״וְזָנָה״." "<b>Further,</b> it intends that it is not that very generation itself that will whore after foreign gods, but the generation that will arise from it. And so it says in the book of Judges (2:8–12): ״וַיָּמָת יְהוֹשֻׁעַ וְגוֹ׳, וְגַם כָּל הַדּוֹר הַהוּא נֶאֶסְפוּ אֶל אֲבוֹתָיו וַיָּקָם דּוֹר אַחֵר וְגוֹ׳ וַיַּעֲשׂוּ בְנֵי יִשְׂרָאֵל אֶת הָרַע בְּעֵינֵי ה׳ וַיַּעַבְדוּ אֶת הַבְּעָלִים וְגוֹ׳ מֵאֱלֹהֵי הָעַמִּים אֲשֶׁר סְבִיבוֹתֵיהֶם״ — and that is what is meant by ״וְקָם וְגוֹ׳ וְזָנָה וְגוֹ׳ אֲשֶׁר הוּא בָּא שָׁמָּה בְּקִרְבּוֹ״."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :or-hachaim, :lang :en, :chapter 31, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T19:20:59.755613621Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}